  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—namely, the probabilities of a favorable outcome and the assumption that outcome differences are negligible—matches what the individual considered. The individual treated the higher amount in Lottery B as not sufficiently compelling to outweigh the lower chance of winning, effectively treating the outcome difference as negligible. Furthermore, the individual’s justification explicitly favors the lottery with the higher chance of winning something (90% vs. 45%), which aligns exactly with the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, both the information used and the reasoning process match the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

