  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on maximizing the probability of a favorable outcome when outcome differences are negligible. The individual does acknowledge that the outcomes are sufficiently similar (aligning with the reason's premise), but then prefers Lottery B, which has a lower probability of winning. Their justification ('setze aufs Glück') indicates a willingness to accept lower probability for higher payoff, which contradicts the rule of the decision reason (which would favor higher probability when outcomes are comparable). Thus, although part of the reasoning (negligible outcome difference) is consistent, the decision rule applied by the individual (favoring higher reward despite lower chance) differs from the reason’s rule. This suggests the reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
}

